{"book":10,"chapter":8,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / GETTING TO KNOW RUST / CHAPTER 8","slides":[{"title":"Your own types","sub":"Chapter 8 · struct, enum, impl","short":"Intro","main":"struct — fields, enum — variants, impl — methods.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Why own types","struct and enum","impl"],"captions":["Big programs need their own types: a user, a point, a color, a status","struct — several fields in one type; enum — one of several values","impl — a block of methods: data and behavior side by side, no inheritance"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"User","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Point","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Status","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"struct\nfields","tone":"green","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"enum\nvariants","tone":"yellow","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl User {","    fn greet(&self) { … }","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[15.2,26.3]}]},{"title":"struct","sub":"Named fields","short":"struct","main":"Declaration, creation by field names, access with a dot.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Declaration","Creation","Fields"],"captions":["struct User { name: String, age: u32 } — fields with names and types","User { name: String::from(\"Anya\"), age: 30 } — give all fields by name, order does not matter","u.name, u.age — field access with a dot; a new type that cannot be mixed up with another"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["struct User {","    name: String,","    age: u32,","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let u = User {","    name: String::from(\"Anya\"),","    age: 30,","};"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"u.name\n\"Anya\"","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"u.age\n30","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.0,24.4]}]},{"title":"Changing a struct","sub":"mut, shorthand, derive","short":"Changing","main":"A field changes in a mut struct; User { name, age }; ..old; #[derive(Debug)].","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["let mut","Shorthand","Update and derive"],"captions":["A field can change only if the whole struct is declared mut; a single field cannot be mut","If a variable is named like the field, write just the name: User { name, age }","..old copies the remaining fields; #[derive(Debug)] enables printing with {:?}"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let mut u = User { … };","u.age += 1;   // ✓"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let name = String::from(\"Anya\");","let u = User { name, age: 30 };"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#[derive(Debug)]","struct User { … }","let v = User { age: 31, ..u };","println!(\"{:?}\", v);"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.6,27.2]}]},{"title":"Methods","sub":"impl and &self","short":"Methods","main":"The first parameter is self; &self reads.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["impl","&self reads","Calling"],"captions":["impl User { … } — functions inside are methods; the first parameter self is \"the one it was called on\"","&self — the method only reads; in the body fields are taken through self.name","u.greet() — called as in Python: data and behavior side by side"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl User {","    fn greet(&self) -> String {","        format!(\"Hello, {}\", self.name)","    }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"&self\n(read only)","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"self.name\nself.age","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let u = User { … };","u.greet()   // \"Hello, Anya\""],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[13.0,25.0]}]},{"title":"&mut self and new","sub":"Change and create","short":"&mut self","main":"&mut self changes, self takes away, new is a constructor by convention.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["&mut self","whole self","new"],"captions":["&mut self — the method changes fields; callable only on a let mut","self without an ampersand takes the instance away: you cannot use it after the call (more in the ownership chapter)","An associated function without self: User::new(…) — a convention, not a keyword"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn birthday(&mut self) {","    self.age += 1;","}"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"&self\nreads","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"&mut self\nchanges","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"self\ntakes away","tone":"red","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl User {","    fn new(name: &str, age: u32) -> User {","        User { name: name.to_string(), age }","    }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[9.6,27.4]}]},{"title":"Tuple structs","sub":"Unnamed fields","short":"Tuple structs","main":"struct Color(u8, u8, u8); newtypes; unit structs.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Tuple struct","Newtype","Unit struct"],"captions":["struct Color(u8, u8, u8); — fields without names, access c.0, c.1, c.2","Meters and feet are both numbers but different types: you cannot add them by mistake","struct Marker; — no fields, serves as a tag; for data, prefer a struct with named fields"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct Color(u8, u8, u8);","let red = Color(255, 0, 0);","red.0   // 255"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"rust","size":11.5,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Meters(f64)","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Feet(f64)","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"Meters + Feet ✕","tone":"red","size":10.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["struct Marker;","let m = Marker;"],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[12.1,21.9]}]},{"title":"enum","sub":"Variants","short":"enum","main":"A value is one of the variants; a typo in the name is impossible.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Variants","Value","Precision"],"captions":["enum Direction { Up, Down, Left, Right } — a value is one of the listed variants","Direction::Up — the type name and a variant joined by ::","You cannot write \"upward\" or pass the number 7: the compiler knows all the variants"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":32.0,"text":"Up","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":32.0,"text":"Down","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":32.0,"text":"Left","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":32.0,"text":"Right","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let d = Direction::Up;"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.5,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let d = Direction::Upp;   // ✕","let e: Direction = 7;   // ✕"],"hl":[0,1],"bad":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.6,26.6]}]},{"title":"Data in variants","sub":"Circle and Rect","short":"Data","main":"Each variant has its own data; together they are one type.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Variants with data","Different shapes","One type"],"captions":["Circle(f64) holds a radius, Rect(f64, f64) holds two sides","Each variant has its own data: in Python you would need several classes","All variants together are one type Shape: the value size is the largest variant plus a tag"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["enum Shape {","    Circle(f64),","    Rect(f64, f64),","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Circle(2.0)","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Rect(3.0, 4.0)","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":260.0,"h":46.0,"text":"type Shape: one of the variants","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.8,23.8]}]},{"title":"match on an enum","sub":"All variants","short":"match","main":"Data is taken out in the pattern; new variants cannot slip by.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Pattern with data","All variants","New variant"],"captions":["match shape { Shape::Circle(r) => …, Shape::Rect(a, b) => … } — data goes into variables","The compiler checks that every variant is covered","Add a variant and every match without it stops building: the compiler shows where to change the code"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["match shape {","    Shape::Circle(r) => 3.14 * r * r,","    Shape::Rect(a, b) => a * b,","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Circle ✓","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Rect ✓","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Triangle (new)","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"✕ non-exhaustive","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[16.1,30.3]}]},{"title":"Option","sub":"Some and None","short":"Option","main":"Instead of null: a value or nothing; match, if let, unwrap_or.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Some and None","No null","How to work"],"captions":["Option<T> — \"a value or nothing\": Some(x) or None","In other languages an empty reference crashes the program; in Rust a value that may be missing is always an Option","match, if let Some(x) = …, unwrap(), unwrap_or(0) — ways to work with it"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Some(5)","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"None","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"null → crash","tone":"red","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Option → check","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["if let Some(x) = v.first() {","    println!(\"{x}\");","}","let n = v.first().copied().unwrap_or(0);"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.1,30.6]}]},{"title":"Result","sub":"Ok and Err","short":"Result","main":"An operation may fail; parse returns a Result.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Ok and Err","parse","Later"],"captions":["Result<T, E> — an operation may fail: Ok(value) or Err(error)","\"5\".parse::<i32>() → Ok(5); \"x\".parse::<i32>() → Err(…)","Details in the error handling chapter; a result cannot be \"forgotten to check\""],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Ok(5)","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Err(…)","tone":"red","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["\"5\".parse::<i32>()   // Ok(5)","\"x\".parse::<i32>()   // Err(..)"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["match s.parse::<i32>() {","    Ok(n) => println!(\"{n}\"),","    Err(e) => println!(\"error: {e}\"),","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[15.8,24.9]}]},{"title":"After Python","sub":"What changed","short":"After Python","main":"class → struct + impl; None → Option; exceptions → Result.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["class → struct + impl","Enum and None","Exceptions"],"captions":["Class → struct and impl; __init__ → new; dataclass → struct with #[derive]; no inheritance — traits instead","Enum in Python is constants; in Rust it is a type with data; None → Option","Exceptions → Result; the \"None has no attribute\" error is impossible: the compiler will not accept it"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"class User","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"struct + impl","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"None","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Option<T>","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"try / except","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Result<T, E>","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.2,22.5]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Summary","main":"Next — the section \"Rust after Python\".","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Remember","Cheat sheet","Next"],"captions":["struct — fields, impl — methods, enum — variants with data, match — handle them all","Option — \"a value or nothing\", Result — \"success or an error\"","Next is the section \"Rust after Python\": we compare every topic in turn and reinforce it"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"struct","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"impl","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"enum","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"match","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["struct P { x: i32 }","impl P { fn new(x: i32) -> P { P { x } } }","enum E { A, B(i32) }","let o: Option<i32> = Some(1);"],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":240.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Python → Rust: types, functions, …","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[11.4,22.6]}]}]}